A||||13||Oreif||Guide to Installing Ocelot Exhaust.||||2||
Z||000000||Oreif||07-05-2001||09:40 PM||||Today I installed the Ocelot Exhaust I bought from the Fiero Store. The install went OK. I am using Rodney Dickmans Cat removal pipe and the Ocelot tips. <BR>Problem #1 The Cat pipe is 2 1/4" Ocelot is 2.0". <BR>Solution: took Ocelt pipe to local shop had it pressed out to 2 1/4".<BR>Problem #2 Due to the previous aftermarket cat set up the cat pipe was too long. Solution: Removed 2.5" from cat pipe.<BR>Problem #3 Ocelot tips. First they look a little small on the rear of a Fiero with the aero effects. Second they are chromed with a soft chrome.<BR>Solution: live with the small size until a custom set I like is found. As for chrome issue, Keep it polished and wax very well.<P>Overall I am happy with the "raspy" sound the exhaust note has. It is louder but I figure I won't be spending a lot of time behind the car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Installation was OK (until we corrected the above). I also found my exhaust leak. The joint right after the cat was cracked 3/4 of the way thru.<P>Hope all this helps someone in the future.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||2
