Z||000007||KissMySSFiero||07-06-2001||11:22 AM||||Gtech....hmmm i need to do that.  what is softer chrome?  is it just a nice way to say cheaper?  =Þ  what are the bends like in the Ocelot system.  are there any crimps?  did you paint it white?  hehe   go get your gtech<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000008||Oreif||07-06-2001||01:10 PM||||"Soft Chrome" is a cheaper process of chroming parts. Simular process to chroming parts on plastic models. The chrome is less durable to the elements and is attacked easily by things like road salt and water.<BR>The bends on the pipes were even and straight.<BR>(No crimps, sharp angles or waves in the bends)<BR>Yes mine are coated white. I may change the section of the tailpipes to silver or black. That is the only area you can see white without going under the car.||||reg||1
